BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Questionable - SAPPHIC EDITION : Queer Singles Trivia
DTSTART:20260923T193000
DTEND:20260923T193000
UID:b839171d71ee0307366541aaba0e54aa@yohomo.ca
DESCRIPTION:Queer trivia served with a side of CHAOS. Is Toronto a tough p
 lace to meet new people? Tired of the apps? Try this! QUESTIONABLE is triv
 ia with a twist…. This is our SAPPHIC EDITION. Always trans and enby inc
 lusive. Already have what you&#x27\;re looking for but have a friend who y
 ou want to set up? Come pitch them! Come be part of the series that has be
 come the stuff of legends..... This event is at GROUND CONTROL 1279 Queen 
 Street West Doors at 7:30pm First Round starts at 8pm Hosted by your faves
 : @chaodykes How does it work? You will be put in a team with 5-6 people y
 ou don’t know. There will be 2 rounds of trivia. Each round\, you will c
 hange teams! So\, by the end of the event you will have met 10-12 new peop
 le. Each round lasts about 40 minutes - just long enough to get to know so
 meone’s vibe but not so long you are stuck with them all night! There wi
 ll be a DJ In the lounge after the event so you can stay after the event t
 o keep the conversations going! What does ‘single’ mean? &#x27\;Single
 ’ means you are open to connecting with other people for love\, lust or 
 friendship. Maybe you will meet your soulmate! Maybe you will meet your ne
 w best friend! Maybe you will make out in the bathroom! Maybe you will add
  a lover to your rotation! Maybe you will find a gaming parter! Basically 
 - you should be available to connect with people in some way. The event is
  poly-friendly\, slut-friendly\, monogamy-friendly\, ace-friendly. If you 
 can’t leave your judgment of others at home\, then you should stay home.
  Schedule 7:30pm - Doors Open\, you get put into your first team 8pm - Fir
 st Round starts 10pm - Expected end\, but you can stay to socialize! Cost 
 We are doing a sliding scale of $7-$25. All funds are going to Glad Day Li
 t to support 2SLGBTQ artists and community events. How will you make the t
 eams? The teams will mostly be random. How many people can attend? Our max
  number for this event is 85 people.This event can sell out and the lower 
 price tickets sell out first\, so act fast. You can email any questions to
  have to: vip@gladday.ca ‍
LOCATION:Ground Control\, 1279 Queen St W
URL:https://www.yohomo.ca/event/questionable---sapphic-edition-queer-singl
 es-trivia-11
X-SOURCE:YOHOMO
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:A Night of Queer Song
DTSTART:20260923T193000
DTEND:20260923T193000
UID:927c8d0b43dd8ec9fe85ba05185aa791@yohomo.ca
DESCRIPTION:Join us for a night of queer song at Three Dollar Bill on Sept
 ember 23rd. Three queer singer-songwriters invite you to join them for a c
 ozy night of music and community as they share their songs and stories. Ev
 eryone is welcome! Arden Van Fleet (she/her) is a trans singer/songwriter 
 from Toronto\, Ontario. Her thoughtful\, wry songs combine classic popcraf
 t and storytelling with a distinctly modern\, queer perspective on love\, 
 friendship\, and growing up. Arden released her debut LP\, Girlfriends for
  a Day\, in November 2025. Maiasha (she/her) is a queer folk singer-songwr
 iter originally from Minneapolis who now calls Toronto home. She is deeply
  connected to her queerness\, drawing inspiration from her own life in her
  lyrics and infusing haunting imagery into her unique musical blend of fol
 k\, pop\, and indie rock. Elina Filice (she/her) is a singer\, songwriter\
 , and storyteller known for songs that defy genre and interactive live per
 formances. Her music is soulful and melodic\, her songs heartfelt and conf
 essional. Now based in Toronto\, Elina has entertained audiences across th
 ree continents. She regards music as a powerful tool for the queer communi
 ty. ‍
LOCATION:Three Dollar Bill\, 1592 Queen Street West
URL:https://www.yohomo.ca/event/a-night-of-queer-song
X-SOURCE:YOHOMO
END:VEVENT
